 ## D6 — evidence and stopping rule
 
 I stopped generator work after the exact final source passed the 12-stage battery, 85 portable tests, the required query-rotation gate, and the 300-lesson census; the proposed direction family also passed all task-local tests and materialized source-bound Racket evidence. No blocker remains. The remaining limitations are epistemic rather than failing gates: finite rivals do not prove unique induction, and no Qwen3.5-9B training experiment was run.
+
+## Current learnability finding: gray-bearing columns
+
+For source `5c2069293d9871570c6d9210941c26a1e3e3cfd4865ddf04b326cc9d1524a157` and canonical rule `4fe6d23687d0`, the bounded protected-Racket probe at `checks/dc050b56cac4/probe.py` found a missing rival: shift down-left by the number of distinct gray-bearing columns. With seed `424242`, difficulty `easy`, and no overrides, demonstrations at indices `0,1,2` have gray-cell counts and gray-column counts `1,2,3`; the query at index `3` has two gray cells in one column. The rival fits all three demos but changes the query, while `lesson_identifiable` returns no reasons. This qualifies the earlier finite-rival no-blocker statement. The retained row-count counterexample still regenerates exactly and refutes all three declared rivals; the old `texture=no_grays` override is now rejected. Evidence: `checks/dc050b56cac4/case.json` and `checks/dc050b56cac4/peer-review.json`; five protected Racket evaluations, no full battery or production export. Proposed repair: add the column-count rival and ensure a multi-cell vertical-stack demonstration when needed, preserving existing witness coverage and query rotations. No generator source was changed; this remains a reviewer finding awaiting owner disposition.
